To change a `nav-link` to `nav-link active` dynamically (e.g., to highlight the currently active navigation link), you can use JavaScript to add the `active` class to the clicked link and remove it from all other links.

Here’s how you can do it:

---

### **1. Update the `handleNavClick` Function**
Modify the `handleNavClick` function to add the `active` class to the clicked link and remove it from all other links.

```javascript
/**
 * Handle navigation link click
 * @param {Event} event - Click event
 */
function handleNavClick(event) {
    event.preventDefault(); // Prevent default link behavior

    // Check if the user is authenticated
    const authToken = localStorage.getItem('authToken');
    if (!authToken) {
        // Redirect to login page if not authenticated
        window.location.href = 'login.html';
        return;
    }

    // Remove 'active' class from all nav links
    const navLinks = document.querySelectorAll('.nav-link');
    navLinks.forEach(link => link.classList.remove('active'));

    // Add 'active' class to the clicked link
    event.currentTarget.classList.add('active');

    // Navigate to the target page
    const targetPage = event.currentTarget.get('href');
    window.location.href = targetPage;
}
```

---

### **2. Attach the `handleNavClick` Function**
Ensure that the `handleNavClick` function is attached to all navigation links when the navigation menu is rendered.

```javascript
function renderNavigationMenu() {
    const navBar = document.getElementById('navigation-bar');
    let navHTML = `
        <div class="nav-header">
            <h2>Michelin Phase 1</h2>    
        </div>
        <ul class="nav-menu">
            <li><a href="index.html" class="nav-link">Home</a></li>
            <li><a href="dashboard.html" class="nav-link">Dashboard</a></li>
            <li><a href="audit-log.html" class="nav-link">Audit Log</a></li>
            <li><a href="settings.html" class="nav-link">Settings</a></li>
        </ul>
    `;
    navBar.innerHTML = navHTML;

    // Attach click event to all navigation links
    const navLinks = document.querySelectorAll('.nav-link');
    navLinks.forEach(link => {
        link.addEventListener('click', handleNavClick);
    });
}
```

---

### **3. Automatically Highlight the Active Page on Load**
If you want the `active` class to be applied automatically based on the current page (e.g., when the user refreshes the page), you can use the `setActiveNavItem` function:

```javascript
function setActiveNavItem() {
    const currentPage = window.location.pathname.split('/').pop();
    const navLinks = document.querySelectorAll('.nav-link');

    navLinks.forEach(link => {
        const linkHref = link.getAttribute('href');
        if (linkHref === currentPage) {
            link.classList.add('active');
        } else {
            link.classList.remove('active');
        }
    });
}
```

Call this function after rendering the navigation menu:

```javascript
document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () {
    renderNavigationMenu();
    setActiveNavItem();
});
```

---

### **4. CSS for `.active` Class**
Ensure you have CSS to style the `active` class for the navigation links. For example:

```css
.nav-link.active {
    font-weight: bold;
    color: var(--michelin-highlight-color);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--michelin-highlight-color);
}
```

---

### **Summary**
- The `handleNavClick` function dynamically adds the `active` class to the clicked link and removes it from others.
- The `setActiveNavItem` function ensures the correct link is highlighted based on the current page when the page loads.
- Attach these functions to the navigation links to ensure proper behavior.

Here’s the correct code to dynamically add the `active` class to a navigation link when clicked and ensure the correct link is highlighted on page load:

```javascript
/**
 * Handle navigation link click
 * @param {Event} event - Click event
 */
function handleNavClick(event) {
    event.preventDefault(); // Prevent default link behavior

    // Check if the user is authenticated
    const authToken = localStorage.getItem('authToken');
    if (!authToken) {
        // Redirect to login page if not authenticated
        window.location.href = 'login.html';
        return;
    }

    // Remove 'active' class from all nav links
    const navLinks = document.querySelectorAll('.nav-link');
    navLinks.forEach(link => link.classList.remove('active'));

    // Add 'active' class to the clicked link
    event.currentTarget.classList.add('active');

    // Navigate to the target page
    const targetPage = event.currentTarget.get('href');
    window.location.href = targetPage;
}

/**
 * Set the active navigation item based on the current page
 */
function setActiveNavItem() {
    const currentPage = window.location.pathname.split('/').pop();
    const navLinks = document.querySelectorAll('.nav-link');

    navLinks.forEach(link => {
        const linkHref = link.getAttribute('href');
        if (linkHref === currentPage) {
            link.classList.add('active');
        } else {
            link.classList.remove('active');
        }
    });
}

// Call these functions after rendering the navigation menu
document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () {
    renderNavigationMenu();
    setActiveNavItem();
});
```

To make the navigation icon (`<img class="nav-icon">`) appear on the same parallel line as the navigation header (`<h2>`), and to make it clickable for expanding/shrinking the navigation bar, follow these steps:

---

### **1. Update the HTML Structure**
Ensure the `nav-icon` is inside the `.nav-header` container so it can be aligned with the header text.

```javascript
let navHTML = `
    <div class="nav-header">
        <h2>Michelin Phase 1</h2>
        <img class="nav-icon" src="assets/icons/account-white-icon.svg" id="nav-toggle-icon">
    </div>
    <div id="profile-icon-container">
        <a href="settings.html"><img class="profile-icon" src="assets/icons/account-white-icon.svg"></a>
    </div>
    <ul class="nav-menu">
        <li><a href="index.html" class="nav-link">Home</a></li>
        <li><a href="dashboard.html" class="nav-link">Dashboard</a></li>
        <li><a href="audit-log.html" class="nav-link">Audit Log</a></li>
    </ul>
`;
```

- Added an `id="nav-toggle-icon"` to the `<img>` tag for easier targeting in JavaScript.
- Placed the `nav-icon` inside the `.nav-header` container.

---

### **2. Add CSS for Alignment**
Use CSS `flexbox` to align the `h2` and `img` elements horizontally within the `.nav-header`.

```css
.nav-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center; /* Vertically align items */
    justify-content: space-between; /* Push items to opposite ends */
    padding: var(--spacing-md);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
}

.nav-header h2 {
    margin: 0; /* Remove default margin */
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    color: var(--michelin-white);
}

.nav-header .nav-icon {
    width: 24px; /* Adjust icon size */
    height: 24px;
    cursor: pointer; /* Make it look clickable */
}
```

- **`display: flex`**: Ensures the header text and icon are aligned horizontally.
- **`justify-content: space-between`**: Pushes the header text to the left and the icon to the right.
- **`cursor: pointer`**: Makes the icon look clickable.

---

### **3. Add Click Functionality**
Use JavaScript to toggle the navigation bar's collapsed/expanded state when the icon is clicked.

#### Update the  Function:
```javascript
function toggleNavigation() {
    const navBar = document.getElementById('navigation-bar');
    navBar.classList.toggle('collapsed'); // Toggle the 'collapsed' class

    // Optionally, change the icon based on the state
    const navIcon = document.getElementById('nav-toggle-icon');
    if (navBar.classList.contains('collapsed')) {
        navIcon.src = 'assets/icons/expand-icon.svg'; // Icon for expanding
    } else {
        navIcon.src = 'assets/icons/collapse-icon.svg'; // Icon for collapsing
    }
}
```

#### Attach the Click Event to the Icon:
Add this inside the `DOMContentLoaded` event listener:

```javascript
document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () {
    renderNavigationMenu();
    setActiveNavItem();

    // Attach click event to the nav toggle icon
    const navToggleIcon = document.getElementById('nav-toggle-icon');
    navToggleIcon.addEventListener('click', toggleNavigation);
});
```

---

### **4. Add CSS for Collapsed State**
Define styles for the collapsed navigation bar in your CSS:

```css
#navigation-bar.collapsed {
    width: 80px; /* Shrink the width */
    transition: width 0.3s ease;
}

#navigation-bar.collapsed .nav-text {
    opacity: 0; /* Hide the text */
    pointer-events: none; /* Disable interaction */
}

#navigation-bar.collapsed .nav-icon {
    transform: rotate(180deg); /* Optional: Rotate the icon */
}
```

